From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: crypto: sun8i-ce - Add CTR, CTS and CBC-MAC for the H616

The H616 crypto engine also does the CTR (symmetric mode 2), CTS (3) and
CBC-MAC (6) modes. Register them for the H616, with the generic
templates as fallback:

- ctr(aes) and ctr(des3_ede): the counter is the whole IV block (counter
  width 128 bits for AES, 64 bits for 3DES), as in the ctr template. The
  counter is encrypted in both directions. A final partial block goes to
  the fallback; the IV of the next request is the counter plus the
  number of blocks.
- cts(cbc(aes)): one request is one complete message, so the "last
  package" flag is always set. One block (plain CBC) and lengths that are
  not a multiple of 4 go to the fallback.
- cbcmac(aes), the MAC that ccm uses: a CBC encryption from a zero IV of
  which the engine writes the 128-bit last block. Only digest() of whole
  blocks runs on the engine, everything else on the fallback.

The engine writes the IV of the next block to the ctr address of the
task. The driver does not use it, but gives these modes a valid one: one
block right after each flow's task descriptor.

The CPU's ARMv8 AES instructions are much faster than the engine, so the
new modes register below every CPU implementation, like xts(aes): the
CPU stays the default and the engine is used when it is asked for by
driver name.

The CFB and OFB modes have no user in the crypto API any more, and the
kernel has no test vectors for a DES CBC-MAC, so they are not
registered. The other variants get CE_ID_NOTSUPP for the new modes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
